Rules-Requires-Root: no

Package: keel-transition
Architecture: all
Depends:
 keel,
 keel-archive-keyring (>= 0.2.0),
 curl,
 gpgv,
 ${misc:Depends},
Description: Move a TurnKey Linux 19.0 appliance onto the Keel Linux archive
 keel-transition surveys a running TurnKey Linux 19.0 appliance, writes
 the Keel instance spec that describes it, and switches its apt
 configuration over to the Keel Linux archive, in three phases that are
 each reversible and each reported file by file (BRIEF section 7):
 .
  * the survey, which is the default, runs keel inspect, writes
    /etc/keel/instance.yaml when it is absent, reports every field it
    could not infer and prints what --apply would change;
  * --apply writes the deb822 source and the origin pin, and disables
    the upstream turnkey.list by renaming it;
  * --rollback undoes exactly that, restoring the upstream list byte for
    byte.
 .
 It refuses to enable an archive whose Release no key in
 keel-archive-keyring verifies, and says so with its own exit code; it
 checks, it does not assume. It never installs, upgrades or removes a
 package: it changes apt sources, one preferences file and the spec.
